  "context_pill": "Partial Integration of Agricultural Income",
  "example_summary": "We calculate the tax liability for Mr. X by integrating his agricultural income with his non-agricultural income across two different age scenarios (40 and 75 years) to determine the impact of varying basic exemption limits.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Partial Integration\n\n| Parameter | Statutory Rule / Condition | Tax Consequence / Treatment |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Agricultural Income** | Exempt under Section 10(1) | Completely exempt from income tax when computed independently. |\n| **Condition 1** | Net agricultural income exceeds ₹ 5,000 p.a. | Mandatory prerequisite for partial integration mechanism. |\n| **Condition 2** | Non-agricultural total income exceeds basic exemption limit | Mandatory prerequisite for partial integration mechanism. |\n| **Senior Citizens (75 years)** | Higher basic exemption limit applies under default regime / optional provisions | Adjusted basic exemption threshold (e.g. ₹ 3,00,000) utilized in Step 1 and Step 2. |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Five-Step Computation Sequence:\n> **Step 1:** Compute tax on (Non-Agricultural Income + Net Agricultural Income).\n> **Step 2:** Compute tax on (Basic Exemption Limit + Net Agricultural Income).\n> **Step 3:** Deduct Step 2 tax from Step 1 tax.\n> **Step 4 & 5:** Add surcharge if applicable and 4% Health and Education Cess.",
